An image path points to a file inside the content root. Entries with media use a directory, and their images stay in a local `media` folder beside the structured fields.

An image field can store alt text with each image. The Astro build treats each image as a local asset: the page gets `ImageMetadata`, or `{ src, alt }` with alt text, so `<Image {...entry.data.cover} />` is enough. Astro optimizes it and emits it with the rest of the static site. There is no media service to secure, monitor, or keep available.
